      "properties": {
        "entityId": "dali",
        "startDate": "0965-01-01",
        "endDate": "1096-12-31",
        "order": 2,
        "segmentType": "other",
        "name": {
          "zh": "羊苴咩城（大理国都）",
          "en": "Yangjumie city (Dali capital)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "羊苴咩城为大理国都。965 年大理遣使向北宋贡方物，宋廷予以册封；1094 年权臣高升泰废段正明自立，国号大中国，1096 年高升泰死，其子高泰明遵遗命还政段氏，段正淳立，大理国进入后理国时期。原「大理—善阐」1096 年路线查无对应行军记录（善阐为大理国东京，但 1096 年无由大理赴善阐的军事行动），已删；1096 年事件由本段都城线覆盖。",
          "en": "Yangjumie was the Dali capital. In 965 Dali sent envoys with tribute to the Northern Song, which granted investiture; in 1094 the minister Gao Shengtai deposed Duan Zhengming and proclaimed the Great China, and on his death in 1096 his son Gao Taiming restored the Duan house under Duan Zhengchun, beginning the Later Dali period. The former 1096 “Dali–Shanchan” route has no corresponding march (Shanchan was Dali’s eastern capital, but no 1096 movement from Dali to Shanchan is recorded) and has been removed; the 1096 event is now covered by this capital line."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
    },
