      "properties": {
        "entityId": "northern-song",
        "startDate": "1120-10-01",
        "endDate": "1121-04-30",
        "order": 14,
        "segmentType": "counterattack",
        "name": {
          "zh": "杭州—睦州—青溪（方腊之乱与官军进剿）",
          "en": "Hangzhou–Muzhou–Qingxi (Fang La’s revolt and the Song counter-offensive)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "宣和二年（1120）十月初九方腊起于睦州青溪帮源洞，十一月息坑大捷，十二月克睦州、歙州并攻入杭州；宣和三年（1121）正月童贯、谭稹率十五万南下，分王禀（自杭州趋睦州）、刘镇（趋歙州）两路，二月围杭州、三月复睦州与青溪、四月破帮源洞擒方腊。本段为整个战事的轴线，杭州—睦州—青溪三点依次对应官军反攻方向；原线作 1120 年九月杭州—睦州，方向与日期均误。路线为示意。",
          "en": "On 9 October 1120 Fang La rose at Bangyuan cave in Qingxi, Muzhou; after the Xikeng victory in November he took Muzhou and Shezhou in the twelfth month and entered Hangzhou. In the first month of 1121 Tong Guan and Tan Zhen led 150,000 men south in two columns under Wang Bing (Hangzhou to Muzhou) and Liu Zhen (to Shezhou); Hangzhou was besieged in the second month, Muzhou and Qingxi recovered in the third and Bangyuan cave broken in the fourth with Fang La captured. The segment is the axis of the whole war, its three points following the government counter-offensive; the former line ran Hangzhou–Muzhou in the ninth month of 1120, wrong in both direction and date. The line is schematic."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
