        "endDate": "1273-03-31",
        "order": 36,
        "segmentType": "advance",
        "name": {
          "zh": "樊城—襄阳（回回炮破樊、迫降襄阳）",
          "en": "Fancheng–Xiangyang (counterweight artillery takes Fancheng, Xiangyang surrenders)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "元军自 1267 年起围襄阳，筑堡于鹿门山、白河口断宋援，围城五年不下。至元十年（1273）正月，阿里海牙用西域亦思马因所献回回炮攻樊城，断襄樊浮桥，破城，守将范天顺自缢、牛富赴火死；二月移炮攻襄阳，一炮中谯楼，守将吕文焕出降。原线起点作「南阳」，查元军出兵与围城记载未见自南阳南下的行军，南阳为后方而非出兵地；现改为樊城—襄阳段，并记围城经过。路线为示意。",
          "en": "The Mongols had besieged Xiangyang since 1267, building forts at Lumen shan and Baihekou to cut Song relief, but the city held for five years. In the first month of 1273 Ali Haya used the counterweight trebuchets of the Western Muslim Isma’il to break Fancheng after cutting the pontoon bridge; its commanders Fan Tianshun and Niu Fu died. In the second month the guns were turned on Xiangyang, a shot struck its drum tower and Lü Wenhuan surrendered. The former line began at Nanyang, but no record shows the Mongol army marching south from Nanyang, which was a rear base rather than a starting point; the segment is now Fancheng–Xiangyang with the siege described. The line is schematic."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
